2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] You're absolutely right! On EC2 instances, the AWS CLI can use IAM Instance Profile
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] credentials automatically - no manual credentials needed if the instance has the right IAM role.
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] Check if your instance has an IAM role:
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] # Test if AWS CLI works without credentials
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] aws sts get-caller-identity
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] If it returns your IAM role info, then you're good to go. If not, you can still use the metadata
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] service without AWS CLI:
2025-10-01 08:01:16 [deepseek-chat] 
