2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] You're absolutely right! That's not professional - using raw IPs in scripts is poor practice.
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] Here's the proper way:
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] Professional Approach - Use Environment Variables
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] #!/bin/bash
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] # Use AWS metadata endpoint constants
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] METADATA_URL="http://169.254.169.254"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] API_TOKEN_URL="${METADATA_URL}/latest/api/token"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] META_URL="${METADATA_URL}/latest/meta-data"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] # Get token and metadata
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] TOKEN=$(curl -X PUT "${API_TOKEN_URL}" -H "X-aws-ec2-metadata-token-ttl-seconds: 21600" 2>/dev/null)
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] INSTANCE_ID=$(curl -H "X-aws-ec2-metadata-token: $TOKEN" -s "${META_URL}/instance-id")
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] INSTANCE_TYPE=$(curl -H "X-aws-ec2-metadata-token: $TOKEN" -s "${META_URL}/instance-type")
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] PUBLIC_IP=$(curl -H "X-aws-ec2-metadata-token: $TOKEN" -s "${META_URL}/public-ipv4")
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] echo "Instance: $INSTANCE_ID ($INSTANCE_TYPE)"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] echo "Public IP: $PUBLIC_IP"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] Even Better - Use AWS Documentation Constants
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] #!/bin/bash
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] # AWS documented metadata service endpoints
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] readonly AWS_METADATA_SERVICE="169.254.169.254"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] readonly METADATA_BASE_URL="http://${AWS_METADATA_SERVICE}/latest"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] TOKEN=$(curl -X PUT "${METADATA_BASE_URL}/api/token" -H "X-aws-ec2-metadata-token-ttl-seconds: 21600" 2>/dev/null)
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] INSTANCE_ID=$(curl -H "X-aws-ec2-metadata-token: $TOKEN" -s "${METADATA_BASE_URL}/meta-data/instance-id")
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] echo "Instance: $INSTANCE_ID"
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 08:06:37 [deepseek-chat] 
