2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] npm install ssh2
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] Then import it like this:
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] import { Client } from 'ssh2';
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] The built-in Node.js modules use the `node:` prefix (like `node:fs`, `node:http`), but `ssh2` is a
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] third-party package that doesn't use this prefix.
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] If you're getting this error in EC2, make sure the `ssh2` package is installed in your project
2025-10-01 09:50:18 [deepseek-chat] dependencies.
