2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] Of course. Here are 15 different approaches for how a summary can be structured:
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 1.  Bullet-Point Summary: A concise list of the most critical facts.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 2.  Narrative Summary: A short, paragraph-form story of events.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 3.  TL;DR (Too Long; Didn't Read): A single-sentence, bottom-line takeaway.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 4.  Executive Summary: Focuses on conclusions, recommendations, and actions.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 5.  Comparative Summary: Highlights changes from a previous state (e.g., "Key developments
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] since June").
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 6.  Topical/Thematic Summary: Groups information by theme (e.g., Politics, Tech,
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] Environment).
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 7.  Chronological Summary: Lists events in the order they happened.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 8.  Analytical Summary: Explains the "why" and "so what" behind the events.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 9.  Visual Summary: Uses a timeline, chart, or mind map to convey information.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 10. Q&A Summary: Poses and answers the most likely questions about the topic.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 11. Key Takeaways Summary: Focuses only on the main implications or lessons.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 12. Quote-Heavy Summary: Uses direct quotes from key figures to tell the story.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 13. Pros/Cons Summary: Weighs the positive and negative outcomes of a period.
2025-10-02 10:54:56 [deepseek-chat] 14. By-the-Numbers Summary: Uses statistics and data points to summarize impact.
